cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ledgerline: a Go 1.26 vs .NET 10 benchmark on a realistic backend workload"
message: "If you quote a number from this benchmark, please cite it and say which run it came from."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Asatryan
    given-names: Haik
abstract: >-
  The same invoicing API, specified once in a frozen spec/ and implemented twice, in Go
  1.26 (net/http, sqlc and hand-written pgx) and .NET 10 (Minimal API, EF Core), against a
  shared PostgreSQL 18.4 and Redis. The measured quantity is cost at a fixed latency
  promise: CPU-ms and steady-state memory per request at the rate where mixed-workload p99
  crosses 20 ms, read from cgroup v2. Load is open-loop and coordinated-omission-safe. The
  published run is 20260814T051533-fedora, config hash
  7889756b00193358a813ff55c42f3e1e806a7cee3bc5d26b65049420b0ec9aaf.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - go
  - dotnet
  - performance
  - postgresql
  - cgroups
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-08-20"
